# system-details cli-json --------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Inferred from origin/main (unreleased). Proposal, depends on$
# §3.11 (not approved: cmd/hardn/output.go:4): hardn system-$
# details --output json. On pkg/output's document, not beside$
# it: --output json is one flag with one contract$
# (docs/reference/output.md), mode "check" already means "read,$
# change nothing", host already holds the name and OS, and$
# wire.go's SchemaVersion comment lets a field be added without$
# a new version. So the nine fields, and one more, details, on$
# this form alone; result nothing-to-do, exit 0. Stock Debian 13$
# has no last, so lastLogin is null and one finding says so. As$
# a user other than root main()'s two lines (cli-not-root) reach$
# stdout first until unit (d) moves them, and the output would$
# not parse.$
$
